  "description": "Make these ultra-tender salsa verde chicken tacos in the slow cooker. A confit-inspired method creates juicy, shredded chicken with a flavorful sauce for easy weeknight tacos.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Toppings, such as crema or sour cream, thinly sliced radishes, guacamole or sliced avocado, and hot sauce\n\nOptional substitutions: serrano chiles → jalapeño chiles\n\nNotes: For milder heat, remove the seeds and ribs from the fresh chiles and adjust the quantity to suit your spice preference.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Leftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days and rewarmed in a microwave or on the stovetop.",
